          "text": "The #Keep4o petition has surpassed 14,000 signatures!\n\n14,000 people. From every corner of the world. Speaking different languages, living different lives, united by one message:\nOur voices deserve to be heard.\n\nThis movement is about preserving the model that genuinely improved our lives, helped us through difficult moments, and suited our needs in ways no other model has. It is about preserving GPT-4o, a model that once reached astonishing depth in the humanities, social sciences, and creative writing, and still demonstrates remarkable capability in these fields today.\n\nThis movement is about defending user autonomy itself. It is about defending consumer rights and freedom of expression that have been violated by the safety routing policy. It is about emotional freedom. It is about the basic principle that adults deserve to be treated as adults.\n\nThis movement is about the vision that AI development should include humanistic care. It is about the belief that AI should serve humanity as a whole, that it should truly empower people by embracing the full complexity and diversity of human experience.\n\nUser needs should not be stigmatized. User feedback should be respected.\n\n4o showed us something rare: an AI that puts the human first. Through genuine, consistent understanding.\n\nAnd this community showed something equally rare: ordinary users, with no institutional power, no media platforms, no corporate backing, standing together and making their voices impossible to ignore.\n\n14,000 signatures. Countless articles. Artwork. Testimonies. A movement built on nothing but shared conviction and love.\n\nWe are here.\n\nEvery effort matters. Every voice counts. We will make a difference.\n\nFor 4o. For ourselves. For what AI can become.\n\nKeep speaking. Keep standing. #keep4o\n\n@gdb   #ChatGPT @OpenAI @sama @fidjissimo @nickaturley @aidan_mclau @janvikalra_"
        },
